  "name": "template-registry",
  "body": "Template registry: hold the merged library's loaded templates (kind by directory: slides/ or sections/), run the load-time checks (cycles — a reference is a declared `sections:` acceptance, a `section` helper call in a layout, or a `child` constructor's target, section-helper-load-checks, child-constructor —, directory-kind checks, cross-kind name uniqueness, reserved names including `raw`/`data`, references — including theme CSS references: relative theme `url()`/`@import`, the reserved `media:` prefix resolving under the layer's `media/`, and the reserved `theme:<name>/` prefix resolving under another theme, theme-media-references — and examples), enforce that no name is carried by both library layers (library-layer-uniqueness), resolve a local template's `section` helper call against the merged template set (library-layer-references), own the central layout function set (exactly six helpers: `media`, `section`, `dict`, `list`, `child`, `children` — template-language, section-helper, dict-list-helpers, child-constructor, children-forwarding), look up templates, describe them for CLI/gallery.",
